## DESCRIPTION
## Dot product between vectors in R^4 as well as dot product between functions on
## [-1,1] and [0,\infty]
## ENDDESCRIPTION


## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Inner products)
## DBsection(Computing with inner products)
## Date(September 5, 2014)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## KEYWORDS('inner product', 'dot product')

# update 2022.10.30

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', "PGcourse.pl");

Context('Numeric')->noreduce('(-x)-y', '(-x)+y');

$a = ColumnVector(random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3));
$b = ColumnVector(random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3));
$ans1 = $a . $b;

($c1, $c2, $c3) = (random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3));
($d1, $d2, $d3) = (random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3), random(-3, 3));

$poly1 = Formula("$c1 + $c2 x + $c3 x^2")->reduce;
$poly2 = Formula("$d1 + $d2 x + $d3 x^2")->reduce;

$tmp =
    6 * $c3 * $d3 + 10 * ($c1 * $d3 + $c2 * $d2 + $c3 * $d1) + 30 * $c1 * $d1;

$ans2 = Real("$tmp/15");

$tmp =
    $c1 * $d1 +
    $c1 * $d2 +
    2 * $c1 * $d3 +
    $c2 * $d1 +
    2 * $c2 * $d2 +
    6 * $c2 * $d3 +
    2 * $c3 * $d1 +
    6 * $c3 * $d2 +
    24 * $c3 * $d3;

$ans3 = Real($tmp);

BEGIN_PGML
Each of the following lists a vector space [`V`], an inner product and a pair of vectors.  Find the inner product of the vectors.

a) [`` V = \mathbb{R}^4, \qquad \langle \vec{u},\vec{v} \rangle = \vec{u}^T \vec{v}, 
    \qquad \vec{u} = [$a], \; \; \vec{v} = [$b] ``]

    [` \langle \vec{u}, \vec{v} \rangle = `] [___]{$ans1}

b) [`` V = \mathcal{P}_2, \qquad \langle p,q \rangle = \int_{-1}^1 p q \, dx , 
    \qquad p = [$poly1], \;\; q= [$poly2] ``]

    [` \langle p, q \rangle = `] [___]{$ans2}

c) [`` V = \mathcal{P}_2, \qquad \langle p,q \rangle 
    = \int_{0}^{\infty} e^{-x} p q \, dx , \qquad p = [$poly1], \;\; q= [$poly2] ``]

    [` \langle p, q \rangle = `] [___]{$ans3}

END_PGML

$poly3 = Formula(
    "$c1*$d1 + ($c1*$d2 + $c2 *$d1) x + ($c1 $d3 + $c3*$d1 + $c2 *$d2) x^2 + "
        . "($c2*$d3  + $c3 * $d2) x^3 + $c3*$d3 x^4")->reduce;
$poly4 =
    Formula("$c1*$d1 x + ($c1*$d2 + $c2 *$d1) x^2/2 + "
        . "($c1 $d3 + $c3*$d1 + $c2 *$d2) x^3/3 + "
        . "($c2*$d3  + $c3 * $d2) x^4/4 + $c3*$d3 x^5/5")->reduce;

$c5a =
    $c1 * $d1 +
    ($c1 * $d2 + $c2 * $d1) +
    2 * ($c1 * $d3 + $c3 * $d1 + $c2 * $d2) +
    6 * ($c2 * $d3 + $c3 * $d2) +
    24 * $c3 * $d3;
$c5b =
    $c1 * $d1 +
    ($c1 * $d2 + $c2 * $d1) +
    2 * ($c1 * $d3 + $c3 * $d1 + $c2 * $d2) +
    6 * ($c2 * $d3 + $c3 * $d2) +
    24 * $c3 * $d3;
$c5c =
    2 * ($c1 * $d3 + $c3 * $d1 + $c2 * $d2) +
    3 * ($c2 * $d3 + $c3 * $d2) +
    12 * $c3 * $d3;
$c5d = ($c2 * $d3 + $c3 * $d2) + 4 * $c3 * $d3;
$c5e = $c3 * $d3;

$poly5 =
    Formula("-($c5a) - ($c5b)x - ($c5c) x^2 -($c5d) x^3 - ($c5e) x^4")->reduce;

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) In this case, we use the standard dot product between vectors in [`\mathbb{R}^n`].  The answer is [$ans1]. 

b) [`\;`]

    [``` 
    \begin{aligned}
    \left\langle p, q \right\rangle & = \int_{-1}^1 ([$poly1])([$poly2]) \, dx  \\
    & = \int_{-1}^1 ([$poly3]) \, dx \\
    & = \left([$poly4]\right) \biggr|_{-1}^1 = [$ans2]
    \end{aligned} ```]

c) [`\;`]

    [``` 
    \begin{aligned}
    \left\langle p, q \right\rangle & = \int_0^{\infty} e^{-x} ([$poly1])([$poly2]) \, dx \\
    & = \int_0^{\infty} e^{-x} ([$poly3]) \, dx \\
    & = - e^{-x}\left( [$poly5] \right) \biggl|_0^{\infty} \\
    & = [$ans3]
    \end{aligned}
    ```]
    where integration by parts was used.

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();    # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
